{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-global-gluing-interpretation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:global-gluing-interpretation","kind":"remark","title":"Global vacuum state and archimedean realisation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-vacuum-state"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-global-gluing","tags":["yekutieli","twisted-quantization","global-gluing"],"text":"global-gluing-interpretation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:global-gluing-interpretation\"></a><p>The <a href=\"#prop:vacuum-state\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/direct-limit\">vacuum state</a> is well-defined globally despite local non-commutativity. In the archimedean realisation, this manifests as the global gluing of the local algebras <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}_{q(p)}(\\mathrm{SU}(2))</code> over the manifold <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/global-gluing-interpretation.md","heading":"Remark","number":"6.6.10","page":"b/rem-global-gluing-interpretation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":45,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":15,"unknown":0,"stale":0}}}
